Every single `reduce` can be replaced with a more intuitive `groupBy`, `partition`, `mapValues`, `keyBy`, etc.Reduce can approximate anything, that doesn't mean we should use it.My favorite antipattern is  items.reduce(
    (acc, item) => ({
      ...acc,
      [item.id]: item,
    }), {}
  );

Like, why? Not only is this ridiculously inefficient O(N^2), it's also longer and less understandable than "build a new map" version.

